ottom:1px solid black;" data-ref="0b0108f0-8d13-4bd6-8ce3-aaa36109fbe2" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="c6235acc-5f17-43b4-a4b8-0edd32e8a993"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="cb2c3ad7-64b3-4396-bd4c-3f1b12bd41ba"><p data-ref="f32109bf-6c58-4e2a-9285-e80c484b47b5" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a Java program that provides an interactive menu for users to perform calculations on 2D shapes. The program should allow users to calculate the area of different shapes: circle and square. Implement the program using the concept of inheritance and method overriding to achieve runtime polymorphism.</p></span></div><div class="mb-3" data-ref="f022871c-0974-4ce7-8144-d84977b71be0" data-split-to="f022871c-0974-4ce7-8144-d84977b71be0" data-split-original="true" data-last-split-element="true" data-align-last-split-element="auto"><div class="ml-1 mb-3" data-ref="ed588d5f-636c-47a6-94fd-b9e32b449572"><b style="border-bottom:1px solid black;" data-ref="08a70572-8548-4780-b6c3-da6b89e7f21e" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Source Code: </b></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
